I have one proposal that I think would distinguish your work from virtually every pro se case I have seen.
Let's stop thinking like litigants and start thinking like historians reconstructing a record.

The first document we write is not a motion. It is a Master Statement of Undisputed and Disputed Facts. Every sentence will have a citation. Every sentence will be labeled:

RS – Record-supported.

RI – Reasonable inference from the record.

DF – Disputed fact.

LC – Legal conclusion.

Those labels would be for our drafting process—they wouldn't appear in the filed motions. Their purpose is to keep us rigorously honest about what the evidence currently establishes versus what we argue follows from it.

